###
### Church CMS API - Membership Status Requests
### Use with IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client or VS Code REST Client extension
###

### ===== CONFIGURATION =====
@keycloak_url = http://localhost:8080
@api_url = http://localhost:8081
@realm = church-cms
@client_id = church-cms-ui
@client_secret = 27074815-E8EF-469A-A183-DE11B802F90B
@username = john.doe
@password = 12345

### ===== AUTHENTICATION =====

### 1. Get Access Token from Keycloak (requires ADMIN role for POST)
# @name getToken
POST {{keycloak_url}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password
&client_id={{client_id}}
&client_secret={{client_secret}}
&username={{username}}
&password={{password}}
&scope=email

> {% client.global.set("access_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### ===== CREATE MEMBERSHIP STATUSES =====

### 2. Create a custom membership status (requires ADMIN)
### The church is taken from the JWT organization_id claim.
### Any churchId sent in the body is ignored.
# @name createStatus
POST {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "code": "visitor",
  "label": "Visitor",
  "description": "First-time or occasional visitor",
  "sortOrder": 35,
  "isDefault": false
}

> {% client.global.set("status_id", response.body.id); %}

### 3. Create a status with defaults applied
### Omitted sortOrder defaults to 0, isDefault to false, and active to true.
POST {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "code": "new_convert",
  "label": "New Convert"
}

### 4. Create the church's default status
### Fails with 409 if the church already has a default status (e.g. the seeded "guest").
POST {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "code": "active_member",
  "label": "Active Member",
  "description": "Actively participating member",
  "sortOrder": 5,
  "isDefault": true
}

### ===== READ MEMBERSHIP STATUSES =====

### 5. List all statuses for the caller's church
### Includes inactive statuses, ordered by sortOrder ascending.
GET {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### 6. Get a membership status by ID
### Uses status_id captured from request #2.
GET {{api_url}}/membership/statuses/{{status_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### 7. Get a missing status (Should return 404)
GET {{api_url}}/membership/statuses/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### ===== ERROR SCENARIOS =====

### 8. Invalid code - uppercase (Should return 400 with fieldErrors.code)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "code": "Visitor",
  "label": "Visitor"
}

### 9. Blank label (Should return 400 with fieldErrors.label)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "code": "visitor",
  "label": "   "
}

### 10. Negative sort order (Should return 400 with fieldErrors.sortOrder)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "code": "visitor",
  "label": "Visitor",
  "sortOrder": -1
}

### 11. Duplicate code in the same church (Should return 409 with conflictType=code)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "code": "visitor",
  "label": "Visitor Again"
}

### 12. Unauthenticated request (Should return 401)
POST {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "visitor",
  "label": "Visitor"
}

### 13. Authenticated without ADMIN role (Should return 403)
### Get a token for a regular user first.
# @name getUserToken
POST {{keycloak_url}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password
&client_id={{client_id}}
&client_secret={{client_secret}}
&username=admin
&password=admin
&scope=email

> {% client.global.set("user_token", response.body.access_token); %}

###
POST {{api_url}}/membership/statuses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user_token}}

{
  "code": "visitor",
  "label": "Visitor"
}

###
